In Pydantic , whichever fields we add , those are by default required fields.
If we skip any field during obj creation , then it wont happen.

to make a field optional , we will have to import typing model

EmailStr - validates email input
AnyUrl - validates AnyUrl

Field Validator helps us in enforcing custom validations on our fields like for example , to check whether an HDFC bank
employee is there or not , we will check his/her email , if it contains @gmail or any other domain , then its not

To do this , we will have to make a new method inside our class , use decorator 

Field Validator operates in 2 modes , before and after 
default - after
after means that the value which we are getting that are after type coercion and vice versa

suppose we are sending 'age':'20' , with before mode , it will give error as type coercion hasnt happend 

Model validatior operates on entire model

computed fields are the one which user doesnt provide explicity , based on the values provided , we calculate the field
